The build bootstrap materializes a modified copy of CodexBar 0.49.3 in
`CodexBar-upstream/`, based on upstream tag `v0.49.3` at commit
`fc57a317cee4a8f84962c62c45e4502085f6fc79`. CodexBar is copyright (c) 2026
Peter Steinberger and is distributed under the MIT License. The bootstrap
fetches its original repository and license before applying the reviewable
patch under `patches/codexbar/`.
The second patch adds an optional isolated cost-cache path and a parser test;
it does not change the default cache or account credential handling.

`codex-reset-usage-pricing.js` adapts CodexBar's MIT-licensed
`Sources/CodexBarCore/Vendored/CostUsage/CostUsagePricing.swift` and
`CostUsageScanner+PricingRows.swift` from that pinned revision. The daily
history interface adapts the behavior of `CostHistoryChartMenuView.swift`.
The bundled collector supplies the normalized local token ledger; the planner
adds independent retention, explicit account attribution and localized day
boundaries. API-equivalent values are offline estimates, not billed charges.

